PART V — ABSOLUTE PLATFORM SEPARATION

13. The three playable platforms must NEVER collide

This requirement is mandatory.

The main cloud and both smaller clouds must never overlap or intersect, regardless of random movement states.

The two smaller clouds must also never collide with each other.

This includes their behavior during:

* Horizontal movement.
* Vertical movement.
* Idle periods.
* Disappearance.
* Reappearance.
* State changes.
* Direction reversals.

Recommended implementation

Give each moving cloud a safe movement envelope.

The left cloud receives a region above the left side of the main cloud.

The right cloud receives a separate region above the right side.

Their regions must remain disjoint, including the platforms’ full widths, heights, and safety margins.

The lowest permitted position of either small cloud must remain safely above the main platform.

Use actual world-space collision bounds, not visual center-point distances alone.

Minimum separation

Introduce a configurable safe distance between platform collision shapes.

Include additional clearance where appropriate for the perspective art.

A cloud’s planned destination must be validated against these restrictions before movement begins.

Also validate each movement step or otherwise mathematically guarantee that the safe movement envelopes make collision impossible.

If a randomized movement would violate a restriction, choose another valid destination or switch to IDLE.

Do not allow the clouds to clip into each other even briefly.

Never resolve cloud-cloud overlap by suddenly teleporting a platform.

Important distinction

Decorative cloud shapes in the background may overlap visually.

However, the three playable cloud platforms must never physically intersect or overlap their gameplay collision volumes.

Visual rendering should also make their separation obvious.

